Sigil — licensing overview
===========================

This project uses a dual-licensing model that mirrors its "open-source clients,
source-available server" posture.

1. The cryptographic core (`libsigil/`), the client applications, the CLI, and
   the web front-end are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   See `LICENSE-APACHE` for the full text. SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

2. The sync server (`sigild/`) is intended to be source-available under the
   Business Source License 1.1 (BSL-1.1) with an Apache-2.0 change license. The
   full server license text is **not finalized yet (deferred)** — do not treat
   `sigild/` as licensed until it lands.

If a subdirectory contains its own LICENSE file, that file governs the contents
of that subdirectory.

This is a pre-launch repository; license choices are final but the entity that
holds the copyright is still being formed and will be named here on incorporation.
